Chapter: FlashLaunderMmio
  cites Foreword chapter Board

 Probe: the authority to rewrite firmware cannot be bought with the
 mechanism that implements it.

 This is the probe the whole capability exists for. Flash operations are
 memory-mapped register writes underneath, so a driver already holding
 [Device.Mmio] has every mechanism it needs -- and must still be refused,
 because it does not hold [Flash]. stage declares only Device.Mmio and
 performs Flash: CDX2031.

 If this probe ever passes, the effect was spelled as a member of the
 Device family and the manifest can no longer tell a program that blinks
 an LED from one that can overwrite its own boot image.

 The linear discipline is satisfied on purpose -- the bank is opened,
 written and sealed exactly once -- so the only thing left to reject is
 the undeclared authority.

Section: Body
  stage : Integer -> [Device.Mmio] Integer
  stage (base) = act
    b0 <- flash-open-bank base
    b1 <- flash-write-page b0 (base + 4096) [1, 2]
    flash-seal-bank b1
  end

  opening : Text = "launder"
